before:
Changing the first margin to 8px leaves a 16px gap, because 16px is now the larger positive margin.
```css
.demo { writing-mode: horizontal-tb; direction: ltr; }
.stack { display: flow-root; } .first, .second { height: 20px; } .first { margin-bottom: 8px; } .second { margin-top: 16px; }
```

after:
The first block sits directly above the second.

```css
.stack {
  display: flow-root;
}
.first,
.second {
  height: 20px;
}
.first {
  margin-bottom: 24px;
}
.second {
  margin-top: 16px;
}
```

The touching margins are 24 and 16 pixels. The gap is 24 pixels.
